//! # GTK CSS Emission
//!
//! Renders a [`Palette`] as GTK CSS `@define-color` declarations. GTK 3 and
//! GTK 4 read `gtk.css` after the active theme, so these definitions override
//! the theme's colors for applications that reference the same role names.
//!
//! ## Generated Output
//! ```css
//! /* Generated by rde-theme; do not edit. */
//! @define-color primary #006A6A;
//! @define-color surface #FAFDFC;
//! ```
//!
//! ## Features
//! - One declaration per semantic role, in the stable order of
//!   [`Palette::role_map`]
//! - Role names match the D-Bus palette keys, so tooling can map either output
//! - Pure rendering: writing the file is the caller's responsibility
//!
//! ## Related
//! - [`crate::domain::palette::Palette`][]: color source
//! - [`crate::backend::qt`][]: the equivalent writer for Qt and KDE
//!
